  "description": "Electrolytic splitting of water into hydrogen and oxygen gases. Alkaline electrolysis (KOH electrolyte, 70-90°C) or PEM electrolysis (solid polymer membrane). Produces ultra-pure hydrogen for ammonia synthesis, semiconductor processing, and fuel cells. Efficiency 60-80%, requires DC electricity at 1.8-2.2V per cell.",
